From 528677cbabd0b1e59a4299475aaabe4aca513e84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:49:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(list view): realtime updates with EventReduce (behind a
 System Setting)

The realtime update of the list view merges the changed documents into
the rows it has and sorts them again. It never trims the list to the
page length and never fetches the row that moves up when a row leaves a
full page, so the list can show too many rows or miss rows until it is
refreshed.

With the new System Setting "Incremental Realtime List Updates" (off by
default), the list view calculates the new rows with event-reduce-js and
its result window buffer. The server event and the permission-checked
query for the changed documents stay the same. The list is refreshed
fully only when EventReduce cannot calculate the result.

Lists with filters or sort fields that cannot be translated keep the
current behaviour.
